    "category": "shrine",
    "name": {
     "en": "Igusa Hachimangū",
     "ja": "井草八幡宮"
    },
    "about": {
     "en": "The guardian shrine of the old villages of Kami-Igusa and Shimo-Igusa. Until the Meiji era it was also called Osonoi Hachimangū, after the area's old name.",
     "ja": "旧上井草村・下井草村の鎮守。明治までは、この地の古い地名から遅野井八幡宮とも呼ばれた。"
    },
    "location": [
