   {
    "id": "ichikishima-shrine",
    "category": "shrine",
    "name": {
     "en": "Ichikishima Shrine (Zenpukuji Benzaiten)",
     "ja": "市杵島神社（善福寺弁天）"
    },
    "about": {
     "en": "The Benzaiten shrine of Zenpukuji Pond, founded by legend in 1197 with a spirit brought from Enoshima. As guardian of the pond's spring it drew rain-prayer processions in droughts, and villages as far off as Nerima and Nakano helped pay for its rebuilding in 1840.",
     "ja": "善福寺池の弁財天。伝承では1197年、江の島から勧請したのが始まり。池の水源の守り神として日照りには雨乞いが行われ、1840年の再建には練馬や中野の村々からも寄進があった。"
    },
    "location": [
     35.716306,
     139.588074
    ],
    "checked": "2026-09-23",
    "source": {
